If a patient has a long-term-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-therapy and a clinician considers a concurrent-therapy-continuation-decision for the patient then the clinician should carefully weigh a benefit against a risk during the concurrent-therapy-continuation-decision.
If a patient has a long-term-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-therapy and a clinician considers a concurrent-therapy-continuation-decision for the patient and a care-team-discussion is appropriate for the patient then the clinician should discuss the concurrent-therapy-continuation-decision with the patient and should discuss the concurrent-therapy-continuation-decision with a patient-care-team-member.
